14"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T18:31:51-07:00","id":516630,"title":"","content":"I think it would be appropriate to go with a Rank 1 Spirit using the rules for one. That way they don't overshadow your Pack Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T23:20:10-07:00","id":516781,"title":"","content":"While I agree that it doesn't seem to likely a spirit joining the pack when they are more powerful than the pack totem, remember that in second edition pack totems aren't as limited in rank as they used to be. <br /> <br /> While a pack having a rank five spirit as their totem is going to be about as common as hen's teeth, I'd just limit the spirit membership to spirits of lower rank than the pack totem. <br /> <br /> Well that and having natures that don't contradict. If your pack totem is a water spirit, then a fire spirit isn't likely to want to have anything to do with you. <br /> <br /> By saying to build it as a wolf-blood or peripheral member, I think the intent was mostly about the points it contributes to the pack totem merit: 1, since spirits can't have merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T05:28:53-07:0